        "typed_refs_valid": true,
        "unverified_claims": [
          "Today's two strongest growth positions belong to memory and agent management. That combination points toward the systems needed to keep agents useful across tasks.",
          "+2,420 stars in 1 day; 41,989 total. Learning-oriented memory leads the ranking, putting accumulated experience at the center of today's momentum.",
          "+2,251 stars in 1 day; 93,960 total. Agent management and memory together gained 4,671 stars—the strongest infrastructure pairing in this snapshot.",
          "+725 stars in 1 day; #20 → #8; 2,277 total. Centralizing model access across agents in a menu-bar interface makes tool-and-model combinations easier to manage.",
          "+381 stars in 1 day; #31 → #14. Extracting, updating and pruning skills from real sessions brings skill upkeep into the working loop.",
          "+326 stars in 1 day; #49 → #18. Local AST parsing and explained graph edges offer a structured way to organize code and supporting context.",
          "+281 stars in 1 day; #32 → #22. Packaging design judgment as a skill makes quality requirements part of the agent workflow.",
          "Stars show attention, not proven effectiveness. But the project mix is clear: agent value is expanding into maintainable experience, knowledge and runtime control."
        ],
